      "message": "**Major** — Extension startup can abort the server with an unhandled traceback, contradicting the commit\u0027s \"never aborts startup\" goal — and it now happens for every user, even with zero extensions.\n\n`_build_extension_context()` eagerly calls `load_gerrit_config()` (line 1676), which raises `FileNotFoundError`/`ValueError`/`JSONDecodeError` on missing or invalid config. Previously `cli_main` went straight to `mcp.run(...)` and config was loaded lazily per tool, so the server still started. Separately, discovery itself is unguarded: `_discover_entry_point_modules()` (`extensions.py:88`) runs outside the per-extension try/except, so a single malformed entry point in the environment also aborts startup.\n\nSuggested fixes:\n- Handle config errors the way `check_config_main` does (clean message + `sys.exit`) rather than a raw traceback.\n- Wrap discovery in a try/except so it honors the stated contract.\n\nReviewer discretion: practical impact is limited to already-broken-config states, so this may be a Minor — but the unhandled traceback and the direct contradiction of the resilience claim are worth addressing.\n\n**Co-Reviewed By: deep-code-reviewer**",
